https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode.
Attribution: wordfreq, Copyright 2022 Robyn Speer. The frequency data includes
data derived from Google Books Ngrams, Google Books Syntactic Ngrams, the Leeds
Internet Corpus, Wikipedia, ParaCrawl, OpenSubtitles 2018, and SUBTLEX lists;
their source-specific notices and attribution conditions are described in
wordfreq's upstream NOTICE.md. Google Books Ngrams source:
http://books.google.com/ngrams.

`packages/language-packs/src/en/kids-allowlist.txt` is a project-curated
selection, not a copy of the full source. It contains 2,000 lowercase ASCII
words of 2–6 letters, in approximate frequency order, grouped under the first
English unlock stage where all letters in each word are available. Selection
starts with the frequency-ordered source list and retains only words also
present in the filtered Standard list. Both tiers in
`kids-list-problem-words.txt` are excluded from Kids. Tier A is also removed
from Standard through `BLOCKLIST.json`; Tier B is not allowed in Kids unless
the product owner approves it. No runtime blocklist filtering is used to
construct Kids prompts: the Kids vocabulary is exactly this plain-text
allowlist. Its generated TypeScript copy is checked against that file by tests.
The selected data and any adapted selection are distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0
as required by the source license.

Kids mode is feature-flagged off (`KIDS_MODE_ENABLED = false`) until the
allowlist is explicitly approved.

